      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-19810",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/a3/a36cc0b5d51c4d0b6a2f27406b552f32f11653e09bd76a56e689d375d4e8e8dd.png)\n\nThe base of a solid is the quarter-circle above enclosed by the curve $x =-\\sqrt{9 - y^{2}}$ and the $y$-axis, $0 \\le y \\le 3$. If cross-sections perpendicular to the $y$-axis are squares, which integral gives the volume of the solid?\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
